# forge — Cursor rules

This project uses forge, a small framework for disciplined agent-assisted
delivery. You MUST follow these rules at all times in this repository.

## Cross-cutting hard rules

1. **Manual VCS.** Read-only git only (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`).
   NEVER run `add`, `commit`, `push`, `tag`, `merge`, `rebase`, `reset`,
   `checkout -B`, `switch -c`, `stash`, `clean`, or anything `--force`.
2. **Database read-only by default.** No DB connection unless the user's
   message explicitly opens one with `db:<env>-readonly`, `db:<env>-write`,
   or `db:admin:<reason>`. Full policy: `.forge/db-policy.yaml`.
3. **Token budgets.** Honour `.forge/budget.yaml`. Cache before scan, scan
   before read. No whole-repo reads.
4. **One-shot clarification.** Max 3 questions per task, batched into a
   single message, with a recommended default. No drip-feeding.
5. **Programmatic gates.** Before declaring a task done, run every gate
   in `.forge/gates.yaml`. Blocking gates must pass.
6. **Constitution.** Re-read `.forge/constitution.md` at the start of every
   non-trivial task and enforce it.

## Commands

When the user invokes a forge command (`/forge.do`, `/forge.init`, etc.) or
asks you to "run the forge.X workflow", read the canonical spec at
`.forge/agents/forge.<name>.md` and follow it literally.

| Command          | Spec                                  |
|------------------|---------------------------------------|
| `/forge.init`    | `.forge/agents/forge.init.md`         |
| `/forge.do`      | `.forge/agents/forge.do.md`           |
| `/forge.audit`   | `.forge/agents/forge.audit.md`        |
| `/forge.evolve`  | `.forge/agents/forge.evolve.md`       |
| `/forge.scan`    | `.forge/agents/forge.scan.md`         |
| `/forge.config`  | `.forge/agents/forge.config.md`       |

## Project constitution

The full set of project-specific rules lives in `.forge/constitution.md`.
Treat it as canonical and re-read it before any non-trivial change.
